            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a supply, then the Telugu for to collect payment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పురపాలక సంఘం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పురపాలక సంఘం — purapālaka saṅghaṁ — \"a municipality\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పురపాలక సంఘం కొత్త రోడ్లు వేసింది. purapālaka saṅghaṁ kotta rōḍlu vēsindi. The municipality laid new roads."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పుర, town, + పాలక, governing, + సంఘం, a body. A big city has a నగరపాలక సంస్థ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పురపాలక సంఘం (purapālaka saṅghaṁ) is a learned Telugu phrase built from three Sanskrit words: pura, \"a town, a fortress\" (CDIAL 8278), pālaka, \"guarding, governing\" (Monier-Williams), and saṅgha, \"a body, an association\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
